1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,027
时钟上排着每晚的三个任务
Three nightly jobs on a clock.

2
00:00:02,347 --> 00:00:04,608
凌晨 1 点准备数据
Prepare the data at 1 in the morning.

3
00:00:04,928 --> 00:00:06,307
2 点训练
Train at 2.

4
00:00:06,357 --> 00:00:07,843
3 点部署
Deploy at 3.

5
00:00:07,893 --> 00:00:09,493
几个月来，一切正常
For months, it works.

6
00:00:11,717 --> 00:00:14,896
后来有一晚，准备数据花了 75 分钟
Then one night, preparation takes 75 minutes.

7
00:00:15,216 --> 00:00:19,290
2 点，训练照样开始，读的是一个只写了一半的文件
At 2, training starts anyway, on a file that is only half written.

8
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:22,639
3 点，部署把训练出来的东西发布了出去
At 3, deployment ships whatever training produced.

9
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:26,137
每个任务的退出码都是 0
Every job exits with status zero.

10
00:00:26,457 --> 00:00:27,836
没有一个失败
Nothing failed.

11
00:00:27,886 --> 00:00:31,470
而 endpoint 现在提供的，是一个只用一半数据训练出来的模型
And the endpoint now serves a model trained on half the data.

12
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:33,390
可也没有一个是对的
Nothing was right either.

13
00:00:33,483 --> 00:00:35,899
课上也从同一个问题讲起
The lecture opens on the same problem:

14
00:00:35,899 --> 00:00:40,032
cheese app 的四个步骤，每一步都由一个人在终端上运行
four steps of the cheese app, each run by a person at a terminal.

15
00:00:40,352 --> 00:00:42,187
这些步骤要怎么执行？
How do we execute these steps?

16
00:00:42,507 --> 00:00:44,150
能不能把这个流程自动化？
Can we automate this flow?

17
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,124
要自动化，你需要一条不同的指令
To automate it, you need a different instruction.

18
00:00:47,444 --> 00:00:49,044
不是：2 点训练
Not: train at 2.

19
00:00:49,151 --> 00:00:51,839
而是：准备数据完成之后再训练
Instead: train when preparation has finished.

20
00:00:52,159 --> 00:00:54,015
这正是 pipeline 的用处
That is what a pipeline is for.

21
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:59,434
接下来的安排：图、连线、重叠、顺序、部署，还有 cheese app
Here is the plan: graphs, wires, overlap, order, deployment, and the cheese app.

22
00:00:59,683 --> 00:01:03,758
右上角的灰色标签，标出每个想法背后的课件页
The gray tag, top right, names the slides behind each idea.

23
00:01:04,078 --> 00:01:05,763
这里没有任何现场运行
Nothing here is a live run.

24
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,781
选项要是在固定时间调度步骤，就想：竞态，时钟对数据一无所知
If an option schedules steps at fixed times, think race: a clock knows nothing about data.

25
00:01:13,117 --> 00:01:17,341
工作流管理，用课上的话说，知道哪一步需要哪一步
Workflow management, in the lecture's words, knows which step needs which.

26
00:01:17,661 --> 00:01:22,226
记录这件事的结构叫有向无环图，也就是 DAG
The structure that records this is a directed acyclic graph, or DAG.

27
00:01:22,467 --> 00:01:26,670
有向，是因为数据只朝一个方向流，从生产者流到消费者
Directed, because data flows one way, from producer to consumer.

28
00:01:26,990 --> 00:01:30,062
无环，是因为没有哪一步会等它自己
Acyclic, because no step ever waits on itself.

29
00:01:30,382 --> 00:01:33,987
这些 task 就是节点；数据依赖就是边
Tasks are the nodes; data dependencies are the edges.

30
00:01:34,234 --> 00:01:37,391
Vertex AI Pipelines 替你运行这些图
Vertex AI Pipelines runs these graphs for you.

31
00:01:37,711 --> 00:01:42,131
你描述这个图用的是 Kubeflow Pipelines，也就是 kfp 这个库
You describe the graph with Kubeflow Pipelines, the kfp library,

32
00:01:42,131 --> 00:01:44,687
而且不用你管 Kubernetes
and there is no Kubernetes to manage.

33
00:01:45,007 --> 00:01:47,780
现在的控制台把它叫作 Agent Platform
Today's console calls it Agent Platform.

34
00:01:48,017 --> 00:01:51,814
这是课件和示例 repo 里的那个玩具 pipeline
Here is the toy pipeline from the slides and the demo repo.

35
00:01:52,134 --> 00:01:55,684
三个标了 @dsl.component 的 Python 函数
Three Python functions marked @dsl.component:

36
00:01:55,684 --> 00:01:57,894
square、add 和 square root
square, add and square root.

37
00:01:58,214 --> 00:02:02,225
第四个标了 @dsl.pipeline，把它们连起来
A fourth, marked @dsl.pipeline, wires them together.

38
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:06,414
在 pipeline 函数运行时，这些 component 调用什么都不算
When the pipeline function runs, the component calls compute nothing.

39
00:02:06,734 --> 00:02:10,955
在 a 上调用 square，a 是 pipeline 的输入，默认值是 3
Calling square on a, the pipeline's input, which defaults to 3,

40
00:02:10,955 --> 00:02:15,310
这会创建一个 task：图里的一个节点，带着一个空的输出插口
creates a task: a node in the graph, with an empty output socket.

41
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:16,967
还没有数字
No number yet.

42
00:02:17,017 --> 00:02:19,812
一行一行地，四个调用放下四个节点
Line by line, four calls drop four nodes.

43
00:02:20,132 --> 00:02:21,690
这里 square 被调用了两次
Square is called twice,

44
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:23,926
所以一个 component 产生了两个 task
so one component gives two tasks;

45
00:02:23,926 --> 00:02:25,892
第二个叫 square-2
the second is named square-2.

46
00:02:26,212 --> 00:02:29,241
这个函数只跑了一次，产出的只有一个图
The function ran once, and produced only a graph.

47
00:02:29,484 --> 00:02:32,407
编译器把这个图压成一个 YAML 文件
The compiler presses that graph into a YAML file.

48
00:02:32,727 --> 00:02:36,490
Vertex AI SDK，也就是课上说的遥控器
The Vertex AI SDK, the lecture's remote control,

49
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:38,764
把它提交成一个 pipeline 任务
submits it as a pipeline job.

50
00:02:39,084 --> 00:02:41,175
你的笔记本负责编译和提交
Your laptop compiles and submits.

51
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:43,095
执行的是 Vertex
Vertex executes.

52
00:02:44,284 --> 00:02:46,291
直到这时，在 Google 的机器上
Only now, on Google's machines,

53
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:49,788
每个 task 才有了 container，数字才出现
does each task get a container, and do numbers appear.

54
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:56,789
选项要是说，在 pipeline 函数里调用 train 就会训练模型
If an option says calling train in the pipeline function trains the model,

55
00:02:56,789 --> 00:02:59,086
再想想：它只是创建了一个 task
think again: it only creates a task.

56
00:02:59,406 --> 00:03:02,286
什么都不会运行，要等到编译好的任务真正运行
Nothing runs until the compiled job runs.

57
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,026
看这个 add 调用
Look at the add call.

58
00:03:05,076 --> 00:03:08,532
对 x，它传的是第一个 square task 的 .output
For x, it passes the first square task, .output.

59
00:03:08,852 --> 00:03:11,454
对 y，传的是第二个 task 的 .output
For y, the second task, .output.

60
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:13,374
那传的到底是什么？
So what is being passed?

61
00:03:13,466 --> 00:03:14,760
不是一个数
Not a number.

62
00:03:14,810 --> 00:03:17,355
这里的 .output 是一个占位符
.output is a placeholder for a value

63
00:03:17,355 --> 00:03:20,890
代表一个只有上游 task 成功之后才存在的值
that exists only after the upstream task succeeds.

64
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,938
把它接上，就画出了一根连线
Plugging it in draws a wire.

65
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:26,561
编译出来的 YAML 把每根连线写了两遍
The compiled YAML writes down each wire twice:

66
00:03:26,561 --> 00:03:29,722
add 的 dependentTasks 列出 square 和 square-2
add's dependentTasks list square and square-2,

67
00:03:29,722 --> 00:03:32,402
每个输入也写明了它的生产者 task
and each input names its producer task.

68
00:03:34,966 --> 00:03:40,278
运行的时候，square 变绿，然后 9 才顺着连线进入 add
At run time, square turns green, and only then does 9 ride the wire into add.

69
00:03:40,598 --> 00:03:44,481
一个参数，就同时给了 add 数据和依赖
One argument gave add both its data and its dependency.

70
00:03:44,716 --> 00:03:47,495
有多个输出时，就点名要哪一个
With several outputs, you name the one you want:

71
00:03:47,495 --> 00:03:50,562
用 .outputs，在方括号里写上输出的名字
.outputs["name"], with the output's name in brackets.

72
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,350
再看对比
Now the contrast.

73
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:56,155
输出本身常常就是一个路径：这次运行写出的文件
Often the output is itself a path: the file this run wrote.

74
00:03:56,475 --> 00:04:00,528
有了连线，train 拿到的正是那个路径，而且是在 prep 成功之后
With the wire, train gets that exact path, after prep succeeds.

75
00:04:00,848 --> 00:04:06,608
改成把路径写死，就没有连线：train 马上开始，和 prep 一起跑
Hard-code a path instead, and there is no wire: train starts right away, alongside prep.

76
00:04:06,850 --> 00:04:10,925
那里的文件是上周的，这一步在过期数据上成功了
The file there is last week's, and the step succeeds on stale data.

77
00:04:11,245 --> 00:04:15,148
猜出来的路径在你看来像依赖，在 pipeline 看来不是
A guessed path looks like a dependency to you, not to the pipeline.

78
00:04:15,383 --> 00:04:18,800
要只管顺序、不传数据，就用 .after 加一条虚线边
For order without data, .after() adds a dashed edge:

79
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:23,596
这个 task 会等另一个成功，但边上什么都不传
the task waits for the other one to succeed, but nothing travels down it.

80
00:04:23,833 --> 00:04:26,478
来做一题。想停的话，就在这里暂停
Try one. Pause here if you want.

81
00:04:32,433 --> 00:04:33,535
答案是 B
B.

82
00:04:33,585 --> 00:04:37,574
点名这个输出，就把这次运行的文件传了过去，也建立了等待
Naming the output hands over this run's file, and creates the wait.

83
00:04:37,894 --> 00:04:39,275
A 把路径写死了
A hard-codes a path:

84
00:04:39,275 --> 00:04:43,484
没有边，所以 train 可能马上开始，读到上一次运行的文件
no edge, so train may start at once and read last run's file.

85
00:04:43,733 --> 00:04:47,893
C 会等，但它读的是你假设的路径，不是 split 报告的那个
C waits, but it reads a path you assumed, not the one split reported.

86
00:04:48,213 --> 00:04:50,671
D 在任何东西运行之前就失败了
D fails before anything runs:

87
00:04:50,671 --> 00:04:54,400
有两个输出时，kfp 不接受单独的 .output
with two outputs, kfp refuses plain .output.

88
00:04:54,650 --> 00:05:00,133
题目说 .output，就想：等上游成功，拿到这次运行的值
If the question says .output, think: waits for success, and gets this run's value.

89
00:05:00,453 --> 00:05:03,823
写死或猜出来的路径：没有边，可能过期
A hard-coded or guessed path: no edge, maybe stale.

90
00:05:04,143 --> 00:05:06,447
.after：有顺序，没有数据
.after(): order, but no data.

91
00:05:07,583 --> 00:05:09,183
回到那个玩具图
Back to the toy graph.

92
00:05:09,268 --> 00:05:12,330
两个 square task 之间没有连线组成的路径
No path of wires connects the two square tasks,

93
00:05:12,330 --> 00:05:15,391
所以 Vertex 可以同时运行它们
so Vertex is free to run them at the same time.

94
00:05:15,633 --> 00:05:17,076
这个 add 是一个汇合点
Add is a join.

95
00:05:17,126 --> 00:05:20,007
它的 YAML 把两个 square 都列为 dependentTasks
Its YAML lists both squares as dependentTasks,

96
00:05:20,007 --> 00:05:22,950
所以它只在第二个完成之后才开始
so it starts only when the second one finishes.

97
00:05:23,616 --> 00:05:27,109
同样的形状，放大一号：一个预处理 task
The same shape, one size up: one preprocessing task,

98
00:05:27,109 --> 00:05:32,214
两个读它输出的训练，再加一个读两个模型的比较
two trainings that read its output, and a comparison that reads both models.

99
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:36,226
一个 task 亮起来，要等每根输入连线都带上值
A task lights up when every incoming wire carries a token.

100
00:05:36,546 --> 00:05:41,815
两个训练一起开始，比较正好在慢的那个结束时开始
Both trainings start together, and the comparison starts exactly when the slower one ends.

101
00:05:42,433 --> 00:05:46,465
加一条数据不需要的边：答案一样，跑得更久
Add an edge the data does not need: same answer, longer run.

102
00:05:47,450 --> 00:05:49,939
把这些连线换成猜出来的路径
Replace those wires with guessed paths,

103
00:05:49,939 --> 00:05:54,469
比较就会在 0 时刻开始，读到没算完的结果
and the comparison starts at time zero and reads half-finished results.

104
00:05:54,789 --> 00:05:56,116
这就是竞态
That is a race.

105
00:05:56,166 --> 00:06:02,054
最大安全重叠的意思是：数据需要的边，一条不多，一条也不少
Maximum safe overlap means exactly the edges the data needs, no more and no fewer.

106
00:06:02,374 --> 00:06:04,486
这样一次运行的时长就等于它的最长路径
The run then lasts its longest path.

107
00:06:04,806 --> 00:06:07,900
如果上游有 task 失败，汇合点就永远不会运行
If an upstream task fails, the join never runs.

108
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:09,750
轮到你算一题
Your turn to compute one.

109
00:06:10,049 --> 00:06:11,649
想停的话，就在这里暂停
Pause here if you want.

110
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:18,950
答案是 B，16 分钟
B, 16 minutes.

111
00:06:19,163 --> 00:06:23,323
最长路径是 ingest、clean、大的那个训练和 compare
The longest path is ingest, clean, the big training, and compare.

112
00:06:23,643 --> 00:06:26,118
2 加 3 加 10 加 1
2, plus 3, plus 10, plus 1.

113
00:06:26,438 --> 00:06:29,830
小的那个训练和 report 都和大的那个重叠
The small training and the report overlap with the big one.

114
00:06:30,066 --> 00:06:32,157
A 把所有 task 依次加起来
A adds every task in sequence.

115
00:06:32,477 --> 00:06:35,186
D 让两个训练一个接一个地跑
D runs the two trainings one after the other.

116
00:06:35,506 --> 00:06:41,032
C 忽略了这些边：训练需要清洗过的数据，compare 要等两个模型
C ignores the edges: training needs clean data, and compare waits for both models.

117
00:06:41,266 --> 00:06:45,063
两个步骤之间要是没有连线组成的路径，就想：并行
If there is no path of wires between two steps, think parallel.

118
00:06:45,383 --> 00:06:49,202
一个步骤要是用到多个输出，就会等齐所有输出
If a step consumes several outputs, it waits for all of them.

119
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:53,379
现在说顺序：预处理、训练、部署
Now the sequence: preprocess, train, deploy.

120
00:06:53,699 --> 00:06:57,006
这里有四种让每一步等待的办法，放在同一个时钟上
Here are four ways to make each step wait, on one clock.

121
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:59,021
第一条泳道：cron 错开时间
Lane one, cron offsets.

122
00:06:59,341 --> 00:07:01,602
第二条泳道：后台的 &
Lane two, background & jobs.

123
00:07:01,922 --> 00:07:06,449
第三条泳道：一个事件在预处理写出输出时启动训练
Lane three, an event starts training when preprocessing writes its output,

124
00:07:06,449 --> 00:07:09,325
部署取实验追踪工具里最好的模型
and deploy takes the best model in the tracker.

125
00:07:09,645 --> 00:07:11,650
第四条泳道：pipeline 的边
Lane four, pipeline edges.

126
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,884
掷一下骰子，决定预处理要多久
Roll the length of preprocessing.

127
00:07:14,204 --> 00:07:15,519
40 分钟
40 minutes.

128
00:07:15,569 --> 00:07:17,119
然后 75
Then 75.

129
00:07:17,169 --> 00:07:18,600
然后 55
Then 55.

130
00:07:18,650 --> 00:07:22,062
时钟那条泳道在 40 没问题，75 就出错
The clock lane is fine at 40, and broken at 75:

131
00:07:22,062 --> 00:07:24,602
训练读到一个写了一半的文件
training reads a half-written file.

132
00:07:24,922 --> 00:07:28,741
后台那条泳道每次都出错，因为什么都不等
The background lane is broken on every roll, because nothing waits.

133
00:07:28,983 --> 00:07:30,818
追踪工具那条泳道错在两处
The tracker lane fails twice.

134
00:07:31,138 --> 00:07:35,212
这个事件可能在第一个文件写出来时就触发，那时预处理还没做完
The event can fire on the first file, before preprocessing is done.

135
00:07:35,532 --> 00:07:39,714
而且追踪工具里最好的模型，是所有运行里最好的，不是这次运行的
And the tracker's best model is the best of all runs, not this run's.

136
00:07:40,034 --> 00:07:42,636
只有边那条泳道每一次都是对的
Only the edge lane is right on every roll.

137
00:07:42,956 --> 00:07:44,556
它只是被拉长了
It just stretches.

138
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:48,137
这个 cheese app 的 pipeline 正是这样做的
The cheese app pipeline does exactly this:

139
00:07:48,137 --> 00:07:55,149
采集之后处理，处理之后训练，训练之后部署，每一步都用 .after
processing after collection, training after processing, deployment after training, each with .after().

140
00:07:55,383 --> 00:07:58,455
在编译出来的 YAML 里，它们变成了 dependentTasks
In the compiled YAML they become dependentTasks.

141
00:07:58,775 --> 00:08:04,194
README 也说得很直白：每一步都要等上一步成功之后才开始
And the README says it plainly: each step starts only after the previous one succeeds.

142
00:08:04,433 --> 00:08:06,097
再来一题，有点绕
One more, a subtle one.

143
00:08:06,417 --> 00:08:09,169
有些步骤只是在另一台机器上启动工作
Some steps only launch work on another machine.

144
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:12,113
记清楚一条边到底在等什么
Remember exactly what an edge waits for.

145
00:08:12,433 --> 00:08:14,033
想停的话，就在这里暂停
Pause here if you want.

146
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:27,201
答案是 B。一条边等的是 task，而这个 task 5 秒后就成功了
B. An edge waits for the task, and this task succeeded after 5 seconds.

147
00:08:27,521 --> 00:08:30,366
这个 pipeline 从来看不到它启动的任务
The pipeline never sees the job it launched,

148
00:08:30,366 --> 00:08:33,857
所以 A 是错的，deploy 可能把上一个模型发布出去
so A is wrong, and deploy may ship the previous model.

149
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:36,233
C：.after 不需要数据
C: .after() needs no data.

150
00:08:36,553 --> 00:08:38,283
D：.after 是强制执行的
D: .after() is enforced,

151
00:08:38,283 --> 00:08:41,311
会作为 dependentTasks 的一项写进 YAML
written into the YAML as a dependent task.

152
00:08:41,550 --> 00:08:44,195
这个 repo 的训练步骤就是这种只负责启动的步骤
The repo's training step is such a launcher.

153
00:08:44,515 --> 00:08:47,230
把 sync 设为 True 之后，它会等自己的任务
With sync=True, it waits for its job,

154
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:52,366
任务失败它也失败，所以 deploy 永远不会在失败的训练之后运行
and fails if the job fails, so deploy never runs on a failed training.

155
00:08:52,686 --> 00:08:55,289
最近一次 commit 把这个等待写明了
A recent commit made that wait explicit.

156
00:08:55,533 --> 00:08:57,622
选项要是用 cron 错开时间
If an option uses cron offsets,

157
00:08:57,622 --> 00:09:01,397
或者后台命令、追踪工具里最好的模型，就想
background commands, or the best model from the tracker,

158
00:09:01,397 --> 00:09:03,149
竞态，或者部署错了模型
think race or wrong model.

159
00:09:03,469 --> 00:09:08,120
从预处理到训练再到部署的边，从结构上就保证了正确
Edges from preprocess to train to deploy are correct by construction.

160
00:09:09,267 --> 00:09:15,111
课上把部署画成五步：拿到保存的模型，更新它的签名
The lecture draws deployment in five steps: get the saved model, update its signature,

161
00:09:15,111 --> 00:09:19,528
上传到 bucket，注册，再部署到 endpoint
upload it to a bucket, register it, and deploy it to an endpoint.

162
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:24,418
签名这一步把预处理搬进模型里
The signature step moves preprocessing into the model:

163
00:09:24,418 --> 00:09:31,138
解码 JPEG，转成浮点数，缩放到 224 乘 224，再调用模型
decode the JPEG, convert to floats, resize to 224 by 224, then call the model.

164
00:09:31,458 --> 00:09:35,831
课件用一种方式保存，repo 用的是 Keras 的 ExportArchive
The slides save it one way, the repo with the Keras ExportArchive.

165
00:09:36,067 --> 00:09:38,392
注册就是建一张目录卡片
Registering creates a catalog card.

166
00:09:38,712 --> 00:09:42,211
它记录文件在哪里，以及由哪个 container 来提供服务
It records where the files are, and which container serves them.

167
00:09:42,531 --> 00:09:44,942
什么都没在运行，也不花钱
Nothing is running, and it costs nothing.

168
00:09:45,262 --> 00:09:46,598
能调用它吗？
Can you call it?

169
00:09:46,648 --> 00:09:50,047
还不能。接下来是 endpoint：一个地址
Not yet. Next, the endpoint: an address.

170
00:09:50,367 --> 00:09:53,613
这个 repo 会复用 cheese-app-endpoint，如果它已经存在
The repo reuses cheese-app-endpoint if it exists,

171
00:09:53,613 --> 00:09:54,834
不存在就新建一个
or creates it.

172
00:09:54,884 --> 00:09:59,044
部署就是在这个地址下面放一台机器，把全部流量都给它
Deploy slides a machine under that address and sends it all the traffic.

173
00:09:59,364 --> 00:10:04,654
从现在起，你要为这台机器付钱，只要它还部署着，即使没人调用它
From now on, you pay for that machine while it is deployed, even when nobody calls it.

174
00:10:05,650 --> 00:10:09,253
预测时，客户端把每张 JPEG 用 base64 编码
To predict, the client wraps each JPEG in base64,

175
00:10:09,253 --> 00:10:11,239
放在 bytes inputs 这个键下面
under the key bytes_inputs.

176
00:10:11,559 --> 00:10:17,384
签名把它解开，模型返回四个分数，最大的那个说出是哪种奶酪
The signature unfolds it, the model returns four scores, and the largest names the cheese.

177
00:10:17,634 --> 00:10:22,349
清理时先取消部署模型，机器就停了，然后删除 endpoint
Cleanup undeploys the model, so the machine stops, then deletes the endpoint.

178
00:10:22,669 --> 00:10:25,463
注册的那张卡片和 bucket 里的文件都还在
The registry card and the bucket files stay.

179
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:28,943
这个 pipeline 的部署步骤做的也是这两个调用
The pipeline's deploy step makes the same two calls.

180
00:10:29,263 --> 00:10:31,259
而按课件的经验法则
And by the slides' rule of thumb,

181
00:10:31,259 --> 00:10:34,767
Cloud Run 适合模型只是一个更大应用的一部分的时候
Cloud Run fits when the model is one part of a bigger app.

182
00:10:35,017 --> 00:10:40,585
题目说已注册，就想：还不能调用，要等部署到一个 endpoint 上
If the question says registered, think: not callable until it is deployed to an endpoint.

183
00:10:40,905 --> 00:10:45,321
题目说已部署，就想：机器一直在计费，直到你取消部署
If it says deployed, think: a machine is billing until you undeploy it.

184
00:10:45,641 --> 00:10:47,284
然后把 endpoint 也删掉
Then delete the endpoint too.

185
00:10:48,433 --> 00:10:50,699
现在看完整的 cheese app pipeline
Now the whole cheese app pipeline:

186
00:10:50,699 --> 00:10:53,297
采集器、处理器、训练、部署
collector, processor, training, deploy.

187
00:10:53,617 --> 00:10:55,857
每一步成功时，都会打上一个绿色的勾
Each gets a green check as it succeeds.

188
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,693
两类步骤
Two kinds of steps.

189
00:10:57,743 --> 00:11:01,223
采集器和处理器是 container component
The collector and processor are container components

190
00:11:01,223 --> 00:11:04,100
从 registry 拉取发布好的 image
that pull published images from a registry,

191
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:08,182
这个 repo 用的是 Docker Hub，课件上是 Artifact Registry
Docker Hub in this repo, the Artifact Registry on the slides,

192
00:11:08,182 --> 00:11:11,460
因为 Google 的机器看不到你的笔记本
because Google's machines cannot see your laptop.

193
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:16,985
训练和部署是 Python component，调用的是 Vertex AI SDK
Training and deploy are Python components that call the Vertex AI SDK.

194
00:11:17,233 --> 00:11:19,793
那为什么用 .after，而不用 .output？
So why .after(), and not .output?

195
00:11:20,113 --> 00:11:22,012
这些步骤从不互相调用
The steps never call each other.

196
00:11:22,332 --> 00:11:24,999
每一步都从 bucket 读，再写回去
Each reads from the bucket and writes back:

197
00:11:24,999 --> 00:11:27,665
raw.zip、clean.zip，然后是 model 目录
raw.zip, clean.zip, then the model/ folder.

198
00:11:27,985 --> 00:11:30,908
这个 pipeline 只决定每一步什么时候开始
The pipeline only decides when each step starts.

199
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:34,721
所以 deploy 按名字在 model 目录里找模型
So deploy finds the model by name, in the model/ folder,

200
00:11:34,721 --> 00:11:36,889
而这些边保证了这个名字是安全的
and the edges make that name safe.

201
00:11:37,209 --> 00:11:40,467
删掉一条，deploy 就可能拿到上一次运行的模型
Delete one, and deploy may grab last run's model:

202
00:11:40,467 --> 00:11:42,328
也就是前面说的读到过期数据
the stale read from earlier.

203
00:11:42,566 --> 00:11:46,289
和课件有一处不同：现在的 main 分支上
One difference from the slides: on the main branch today,

204
00:11:46,289 --> 00:11:51,057
训练会自己下载数据集，所以这些边传的是顺序，不是数据
training downloads its own dataset, so these edges carry order, not data.

205
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:55,396
在 AWS 上，SageMaker Pipelines 用的是同一个思路
On AWS, SageMaker Pipelines runs the same idea.

206
00:11:55,716 --> 00:11:59,986
训练步骤的输入指向处理步骤的输出属性
The training step's input points at the processing step's output property,

207
00:11:59,986 --> 00:12:01,774
这个引用就是边
and that reference is the edge.

208
00:12:02,266 --> 00:12:04,449
把 pipeline 的步骤列表打乱
Shuffle the pipeline's list of steps,

209
00:12:04,449 --> 00:12:08,048
图也不会动：顺序来自引用
and the graph does not move: order comes from the references.

210
00:12:08,283 --> 00:12:12,294
题目说 SageMaker Pipelines，就想：同一个 DAG
If the question says SageMaker Pipelines, think: the same DAG.

211
00:12:12,614 --> 00:12:15,131
引用一个步骤的属性，就造出了边
Referencing a step's properties makes the edge.

212
00:12:16,267 --> 00:12:17,668
七条规则
Seven rules.

213
00:12:17,718 --> 00:12:19,446
第一条：pipeline 是 DAG
One: pipelines are DAGs.

214
00:12:19,766 --> 00:12:22,521
调用一个 component 就创建一个 task，即一个节点
Calling a component creates a task, a node.

215
00:12:22,710 --> 00:12:25,590
什么都不会运行，要等到编译好的任务真正运行
Nothing runs until the compiled job runs.

216
00:12:25,834 --> 00:12:28,164
第二条：.output，或者一个有名字的输出
Two: .output, or a named output,

217
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:31,295
会造出边，并传递这次运行的值
makes the edge and passes this run's value.

218
00:12:31,615 --> 00:12:34,858
第三条：猜出来的路径不会造出边，还可能是过期的
Three: a guessed path makes no edge, and may be stale.

219
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:37,617
第四条：.after 只排顺序，不传数据
Four: .after() orders without data.

220
00:12:37,937 --> 00:12:40,987
第五条：task 之间没有路径就是并行
Five: no path between tasks means parallel,

221
00:12:40,987 --> 00:12:45,810
汇合点要等齐所有输入，一次运行的时长等于它的最长路径
a join waits for all its inputs, and the run lasts its longest path.

222
00:12:46,050 --> 00:12:51,576
第六条：顺序来自边，不来自时钟；启动了工作的步骤必须等它完成
Six: order comes from edges, not clocks, and a step that launches work must wait for it.

223
00:12:51,817 --> 00:12:54,231
第七条：上传到 Model Registry
Seven: upload to the Model Registry,

224
00:12:54,231 --> 00:12:56,980
创建一个 endpoint，部署，然后预测
create an endpoint, deploy, then predict.

225
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:58,900
计费从部署开始
Billing starts at deploy.

226
00:12:59,177 --> 00:13:02,569
SageMaker 用步骤属性搭出同一个 DAG
SageMaker builds the same DAG from step properties.

227
00:13:02,817 --> 00:13:07,694
还有课上的那条链：用 DSL 写的配方，印成 YAML
And the lecture's chain: a recipe in the DSL, printed as YAML,

228
00:13:07,694 --> 00:13:11,548
由 SDK 提交，在 Kubeflow 引擎上运行
submitted by the SDK, run on the Kubeflow engine,

229
00:13:11,548 --> 00:13:16,662
由 Vertex AI Pipelines 托管，不用自己搭 Kubernetes
and managed by Vertex AI Pipelines, with no Kubernetes to set up.

230
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:19,887
用完之后，取消部署，再删除 endpoint
When you are done, undeploy and delete the endpoint.

231
00:13:20,207 --> 00:13:21,807
祝你小测顺利
Good luck on the quiz.
